# Checks an engine cannot pass for reasons outside tekx, one per line:
#	ENGINE CHECK REASON
# test/paste.sh reports these as limits rather than failures, and says so
# when one starts passing.  A formula is named by its line in
# test/formulas.txt:	ENGINE formula N REASON
#
# pdf.js (Firefox) reads only the glyphs and their invisible helpers: it
# ignores ActualText (pdf.js 6.5), which poppler, PDFium and Acrobat honour.
pdfjs prose a word hyphenated across lines pastes as its two halves, since only ActualText holds the whole word
pdfjs formula 20 the brace of cases is a visible { glyph, so the paste reads {x, if x ≥ 0; −x, otherwise
pdfjs formula 23 a root's radical is a visible √, so root 3 of x pastes as root(3, √x)
pdfjs formula 34 −∂B⃗ has no visible gap where the copy text has (−∂ B⃗), so it reads back as −(∂B⃗): the same quantity, grouped differently
